WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.240
He's a near-unstoppable force of evil so dangerous&nbsp;
that on multiple occasions, Spider-Man and Venom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.880
have been forced to set aside their differences&nbsp;
to put an end to his wrath. Let's take a look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.920
at the chaotic mind and twisted motivations of&nbsp;
Carnage, one of Marvel's deadliest villains.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.480
Carnage is the product of the bond between&nbsp;
a member of the symbiotic alien race known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.880
as the Klyntar and Cletus Kasady, a&nbsp;
deranged serial killer who pushed his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.280
own grandmother down a flight of stairs as&nbsp;
a child. Casady was sent to an orphanage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:33.920
which he burned down. So he developed a lust&nbsp;
for pure chaos and mayhem long before he ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.960
came into contact with the symbiote. So when&nbsp;
artists Erik Larsen and Mark Bagley were seeking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.120
inspiration for the character's appearance&nbsp;
and traits, they didn't have to look far.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:48.480
Writer David Michelinie conceived of Carnage as&nbsp;
the closest thing to an irredeemably malevolent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.440
force as could exist in the Marvel Universe,&nbsp;
so the artists modeled Kasady on the Joker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.040
who has long filled just such&nbsp;
a role in the DC Universe.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:00.640
"I'm a dog chasing cars. I wouldn't&nbsp;
know what to do with one if I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.000
caught it. You know, I just do things."

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.040
Eddie Brock, separated from his Venom&nbsp;
symbiote and sent to prison for his crimes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:12.720
was Kasady's cellmate. While waiting&nbsp;
for the symbiote to spring him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.720
Brock developed an antagonistic&nbsp;
attitude toward the depraved Kasady,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:21.760
beating him mercilessly on more than one occasion.&nbsp;
The Venom symbiote did eventually manage to free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:26.880
Brock. But in the process, it spawned a new&nbsp;
symbiote, leaving it behind in Kasady's cell.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.920
This technically makes Carnage Venom's son. Unlike&nbsp;
the contentious bond Brock shares with Venom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:37.040
in which the two sometimes duel for control,&nbsp;
Carnage sees its relationship with Kasady as more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:42.000
than symbiotic. It entered Kasady's body through&nbsp;
a cut, so the symbiote was able to bond with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.520
bloodstream, making the two extremely difficult&nbsp;
to separate. Unlike Venom, Carnage does not refer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:52.800
to itself as "we." It's one entity. Venom's&nbsp;
hatred of Carnage is so intense that it even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:58.000
overrides his hatred of Spider-Man. And as far&nbsp;
as Carnage is concerned, the feeling is mutual.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:02.960
It might be tough to separate Carnage from&nbsp;
Kasady, but it has happened a few times.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:07.040
And when it has, Carnage had no problem&nbsp;
bonding with other hosts. Its unpowered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:12.800
victims through the multiverse have included&nbsp;
Gwen Stacy, John Jameson, and Dr. Tanis Nieves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:18.320
the psychiatrist of Carnage's "girlfriend" Shriek.&nbsp;
Carnage has also bonded with superpowered people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:23.520
a truly terrifying proposition. For one, it&nbsp;
bonded with Ben Reilly, Spider-Man at the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:28.960
to create Spider-Carnage. The symbiote also once&nbsp;
briefly bonded with the extremely powerful Silver&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:33.920
Surfer to become Carnage Cosmic. In one of&nbsp;
Peter Parker's worst nightmares come true,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:39.200
Carnage also once bonded with Norman Osborn,&nbsp;
the Green Goblin, to become the Red Goblin.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:44.160
Already greatly enhanced by his Goblin serum,&nbsp;
Osborn became exponentially more powerful with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:49.360
Carnage. Obsessed not just with killing Spider-Man&nbsp;
but crushing his very soul, the Goblin threatened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:54.880
to slowly and painfully kill everyone Peter held&nbsp;
dear unless he gave up his crime-fighting ways.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:59.360
After a brawl that left the Daily Bugle&nbsp;
offices in shambles and Flash Thompson dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:03.680
Parker revealed his desperation by allowing&nbsp;
the Venom symbiote to bond with him for one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:08.240
last shot at victory over the Red Goblin. On&nbsp;
the brink of death, Peter was able to convince&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:12.640
Osborn that Carnage, not the Goblin, would&nbsp;
get all the credit for killing Spider-Man.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:17.840
Driven by ego, Osborn shredded the symbiote,&nbsp;
which led to the villain's sound defeat.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:21.680
Klyntar are generally indifferent or&nbsp;
antagonistic toward their offspring,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:26.800
and Carnage is no exception. During the brief&nbsp;
time the symbiote was in control of Dr. Nieves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:31.840
it used her to find Kasady, abandoning her for&nbsp;
his original host but leaving its spawn behind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:36.480
growing on her arm. Horrified, Nieves took&nbsp;
drastic action and cut her arm off. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:41.280
symbiotes don't give up easily, and it eventually&nbsp;
re-bonded with her to become the heroic Scorn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.720
who has been a thorn in the side of&nbsp;
her "father" on multiple occasions.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:48.880
Another of Carnage's offspring was&nbsp;
outright rejected. Carnage, disgusted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:53.280
and enraged by its spawn, implanted it into&nbsp;
New York police officer "Paddy" Mulligan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:57.200
during a chance encounter. Resolving to&nbsp;
kill it before it could reach maturity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:02.160
Carnage attacked Mulligan and his family,&nbsp;
but was foiled by Spider-Man and Black Cat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:07.360
Mulligan tracked the Cat down for answers, but&nbsp;
the pair once again came under attack by Carnage.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:11.360
This time, the new symbiote made its&nbsp;
presence known. Calling itself Toxin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:15.840
it single-handedly took down both Carnage&nbsp;
and Venom, and resolved to become a hero.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:20.880
The virtuous Mulligan had trouble containing the&nbsp;
symbiote's homicidal urges, however, and after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:26.240
officer was killed in battle, Toxin briefly bonded&nbsp;
with Eddie Brock, and finally with Bren Waters.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:31.440
Venom and Carnage have battled countless times,&nbsp;
with the latter's superior strength usually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:36.320
giving him the upper hand. But Venom has often&nbsp;
outsmarted him. At one point, Kasady was being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:41.120
held in a special prison designed to contain&nbsp;
Carnage when Venom paid his "son" a visit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:45.840
Kasady could only gibber helplessly as Venom&nbsp;
ripped the symbiote from his body and devoured it.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:50.240
Kasady escaped and attempted to resume his&nbsp;
reign of terror by painting himself red and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:54.880
embarking on yet another killing spree as a&nbsp;
makeshift "Carnage." He was easily defeated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:59.040
by Spider-Man, but Kasady was given new&nbsp;
hope. A failed invasion of Earth by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:02.880
interdimensional beings of the Negative&nbsp;
Zone reactivated dormant traces of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:06.880
symbiote within his bloodstream. Finding his&nbsp;
way through a portal to the Negative Zone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:12.160
Kasady was mysteriously guided to a second&nbsp;
symbiote, apparently identical to his first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.240
and enthusiastically allowed it to bond&nbsp;
with him, becoming Carnage once again.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:21.680
During the events of the Avengers/X-Men AXIS&nbsp;
crossover event, the moral alignments of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:26.560
number of heroes and villains were magically&nbsp;
switched. This had a profound effect on Carnage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:31.760
who found himself saddled with an overwhelming&nbsp;
desire to help people and do good despite having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:36.800
literally no idea how. He abducted local&nbsp;
reporter Alice Gleason to tutor him in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:41.440
ways of being a hero after barely restraining&nbsp;
himself from killing a couple of random thugs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:45.600
But even under her strict guidance,&nbsp;
Carnage tended to get his wires crossed.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:50.240
For example, when Carnage and Alice came across&nbsp;
a bank being robbed, the symbiote heroically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:55.440
thwarted the robbery — before attempting to burn&nbsp;
down the bank to prevent future robberies. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.440 --> 00:06:00.240
apparently developing romantic feelings for Alice,&nbsp;
Carnage was constantly distracted by fantasies of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:05.840
her dying. During a climactic battle in New York,&nbsp;
Carnage apparently sacrificed himself for the good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:11.120
of the city. But of course, such deaths are almost&nbsp;
always temporary in the Marvel Universe — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:15.680
it wouldn't be long before Kasady appeared&nbsp;
once again, back to his old homicidal ways.

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:20.000
Marvel's Ultimate line of comics,&nbsp;
which began publication in 2000,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:25.200
updated some of its most popular characters and&nbsp;
storylines for a new generation of readers. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:28.800
took place in a different continuity&nbsp;
than the mainstream Marvel Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:33.680
and while it is now defunct, some of its more&nbsp;
popular original characters, namely Miles Morales,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:38.240
managed to survive the destruction of their home&nbsp;
universe, and have come over to the main Marvel U.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:43.040
"So I'm Spider-Man. I'm not the only one."

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:48.640
In the Ultimate universe, symbiotes weren't an&nbsp;
alien race. Instead, they were the result of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:53.840
a genetic experiment by Peter Parker's father,&nbsp;
Richard, and Eddie Brock, Sr. The first of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:58.320
symbiotes was Venom, and its relationship&nbsp;
to Peter and Eddie Jr. played out much the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:04.080
same way it did in the main continuity. Carnage,&nbsp;
however, was created in a lab by Dr. Curt Connors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:08.640
who had the bright idea to combine some&nbsp;
of Peter's DNA with a sample of Venom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:13.120
along with his own Lizard-mutated DNA. The&nbsp;
result was a fearsome beast which could only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:18.080
survive by feeding on humans, and was obsessed&nbsp;
with consuming Spider-Man to complete its DNA&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:22.800
sequence. It even ate Gwen Stacy, then&nbsp;
created an exact genetic replica of her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:27.600
to serve as its host. This version of Carnage&nbsp;
was itself eventually consumed by Venom.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:32.000
On a couple of the rare occasions in which&nbsp;
Marvel has teamed up with rival publisher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:37.680
DC for crossovers, Carnage has been involved. He&nbsp;
notably teamed up with his inspiration, the Joker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:43.520
for the 1995 one-shot "Spider-Man and Batman:&nbsp;
Disordered Minds." The teamup was short-lived;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:46.960
although they seem like the perfect&nbsp;
evil pairing, Carnage butted heads&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:51.360
with the Clown Prince of Crime early and&nbsp;
often due to the Joker's tendency toward&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:56.320
theatrics and his own preference for wanton&nbsp;
slaughter. Carnage found the Joker's methods&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.320 --> 00:08:00.800
to be tedious and unsatisfying, while&nbsp;
the Joker found Carnage to be a hack.

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:05.520
Carnage also made his presence known in the&nbsp;
Amalgam line of comics, an imprint in which Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:10.640
and DC heroes and villains were combined to create&nbsp;
new mashup characters. Carnage was mashed up with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:16.480
Superman nemesis Bizarro to create Bizarnage. The&nbsp;
creature wreaked indiscriminate havoc until it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:22.000
eventually tricked and defeated by Spider-Boy,&nbsp;
himself a mashup of Spider-Man and Superboy.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:26.720
Carnage's surprise cameo in the 2018&nbsp;
"Venom" feature film promised that...

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:28.880
"There's gonna be carnage."

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:33.920
It raised the character's profile, so Marvel&nbsp;
brought him back to the comics page with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:38.800
the "Web of Venom: Carnage Born" one-shot. Its&nbsp;
story deals with a cult attempting to resurrect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:42.960
the villain after his death in the "Venomized"&nbsp;
storyline. And if that's not dark enough, it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:48.320
implied Kasady was a cannibal before fusing with&nbsp;
the symbiote. The issue's solicitation states,

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:51.120
"A cruel cannibal obsessed with death and murder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:55.040
few mourned Cletus Kasady after&nbsp;
he seemingly died in VENOMIZED."

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:59.120
With the second Venom movie subtitled&nbsp;
"Let There Be Carnage," it's no surprise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:03.360
Marvel comics giving us a revamped and&nbsp;
even darker version of the character.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:07.760
Though it should be noted Carnage had some&nbsp;
pretty dark comics appearances well before.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:11.760
"Venom: Let There Be Carnage" is primed to&nbsp;
give us a cinematic villain for the ages,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:15.360
and it certainly doesn't hurt that the&nbsp;
great Woody Harrelson is filling the role.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:20.880
Carnage has starred in plenty of miniseries,&nbsp;
one-shots, and even line-wide events based on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:27.120
his bloody exploits, but the release of 2016's&nbsp;
"Carnage" #1 gave the crazed symbiote his first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:32.000
ongoing monthly series. It also marked&nbsp;
the Marvel return of writer Gerry Conway,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:35.040
his first work on a regular&nbsp;
Marvel series since the '90s.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:39.600
The series finds the title villain lured to&nbsp;
Grey Ridge Mine with Manuela Calderon — the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:44.960
sole survivor of Cletus Kasady's very first mass&nbsp;
killing — as bait. But when the owner of the mine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:49.600
turns out to have his own agenda, Carnage and some&nbsp;
of the agents tasked with capturing him fall into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:55.600
the mine. Calderon, Eddie Brock, John Jameson,&nbsp;
and FBI Special Agent Claire Dixon follow Carnage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:59.840
into the depths, where a strange cult called&nbsp;
the Darkholders wait with their own plans.

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:04.640
Most of the series' 16 issues revolve around&nbsp;
an unexpected mystical and prophetic connection&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:09.680
between Carnage and an ancient Lovecraftian&nbsp;
god. Before the end, Carnage gets a power boost,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:13.280
and one of the heroes chasing him becomes&nbsp;
part of the violent symbiote family.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:18.640
In the "Venom" series that debuted in 2018,&nbsp;
it's revealed the Klyntar symbiotes are not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:24.240
just an alien species, but parasites created&nbsp;
by the eldritch god Knull to do his bidding.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:28.240
So after the Cult of Knull resurrects&nbsp;
Carnage in "Web of Venom: Carnage Born,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:31.920
they reveal that every human on Earth to&nbsp;
ever bond with a symbiote has what they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:36.160
call a "codex" embedded in their DNA.&nbsp;
If Carnage collects all these codexes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:39.920
he will become the vessel for Knull on&nbsp;
Earth and be able to conquer the world.

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:44.880
After a lot of bloodshed, including the deaths&nbsp;
of a superhero or two, Venom kills Cletus in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:51.280
2020's "Absolute Carnage" #5. But in doing so,&nbsp;
ensures the eventual assault on Earth by Knull.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:55.760
Venom has to resolve that in the "King in Black"&nbsp;
event, where Carnage plays only a small role.

00:10:56.560 --> 00:11:00.400
Carnage became a meal for sharks in "Carnage:&nbsp;
Black, White and Blood," but "Extreme&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:04.880
Carnage Alpha" #1 reveals that a piece of the&nbsp;
symbiote survived at the bottom of the ocean.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:09.760
It bonds with a fish and works its way up the&nbsp;
chain to eventually bond with xenophobic Senator&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:15.520
Peter Krane, who's seeking an end to "harboring"&nbsp;
any and all extraterrestrial aliens on U.S. soil.

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:19.520
Carnage uses Senator Krane's voice to&nbsp;
seize the wills of various symbiotes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:23.680
over the television airwaves. Standing&nbsp;
against them are Flash Thompson — now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:28.560
Agent Anti-Venom — and Andi Benton,&nbsp;
the former host of the symbiote Scream.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:32.880
After crippling her symbiote with hellfire&nbsp;
to stop it from following Carnage's orders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:37.440
she rebonds with an altered version of&nbsp;
the symbiote, now calling itself Silence.

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:40.720
Check out one of our newest&nbsp;
videos right here! Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:44.720
even more Looper videos about your&nbsp;
favorite Marvel characters are coming soon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:54.560
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit&nbsp;
the bell so you don't miss a single one.

